 issues:\r\n\r\n3D transform gizmos are broken, they don't show.\r\n\r\nFloating 3D editor right click freelook mouse position is not correct when finishing.\r\n\r\nFloating 2D editor panning is broken.\r\n\r\nClosing or floating all main docks and clicking the main screen's dock context popup button crashes.\r\n\r\nWith the editors floating, it should focus them when they are being edited. For example clicking on a script (from scene dock or filesystem) doesn't open the script editor, and clicking on a 3D node does not bring up the 3D editor. Or if can't focus for some reason at least `window_move_to_foreground`.\r\nThis also applies to 2D and 3D when they are closed, but maybe that is intentional.\r\nBut if that is the case then 2D and 3D editors probably shouldn't open on scene change if they were closed.\r\n\r\nIf the 2D editor is floating or closed then docks like GridMap, TileMap, Animation, Polygon2D, etc don't open.\r\n\r\nThis makes it harder to access the script editor when it is floating since the button is removed. Same with making it floating since its an extra click and in a menu. Not sure if there is anything to be done about it though.\r\n\r\nClosing or floating all main docks shows a big empty space, which is unlike closing other docks. Not sure what to do about it especially since bottom panel can be minimized.\r\n\r\nIts kind of weird to have the tab bar dock context menu button off to the right, far away from the main docks.\r\n\r\n<img width=\"1913\" height=\"46\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3806a6f1-cb97-46b0-9376-e0bae064b9fe\" />\r\n\r\nNot sure if it would be better right next to them though.\r\nAnd it may have changed the centering slightly, the logic for it may need to be updated.\r\n\r\nRecovery mode crashes. I'm guessing its related to the Game view not being available.","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113051#pullrequestreview-3873749447","pull_request_url":"htt